tmp-probe/

# The full 20-face glyph table (1.2 MB) is a build intermediate, not a
# deliverable. `scripts/generate-glyphs.ts` regenerates it byte-identically from
# the pinned `katex` devDependency's TTFs, so a plain `bun install` is enough —
# verified identical across all 20 fonts to the upstream repository's copies.
# Only the subset it feeds is committed, and both stages of that subset are:
# `src/glyphs/glyphs.subset.json` is the human-readable build input, and
# `src/glyphs/glyphs.subset.ts` is the compact binary table `src/emit/glyphTable.ts`
# actually imports at runtime. Both are committed so the package builds without
# running any generator, and so `encode-glyphs --check` can prove in CI that the
# shipped table still matches its input.
src/glyphs/glyphs.json
